# The slot-less half of R-AE: a fresh walrus with no store to take a type from is `x = None`'s
# refusal, and the steer names BOTH spellings of absence. It cannot say `q: T? = None`, which R-G
# (#1720) refuses — a Sharpy optional is built with None().
#
# `print((q := None))` is NOT this cell: `print`'s parameter is an `object` slot, so the walrus is
# the direct operand of a store and takes it (R-AE). That program prints `None` twice, exactly as
# python3 does; it is the last two lines of basics/fresh_walrus_under_slot_1812.
def main() -> None:
    x = (q := None)
    print(x)
